                  <provenance type="#e"><orgName role="fmo" key="mlgbOrg_426">Oxford, Oxfordshire.
                        Balliol College (Domus de Balliolo)</orgName><p>‘&lt;Liber scholarium de
                        Ball&gt;iolo per magistrum Willelmum de Mundham in quo continentur Tabula
                        moralium Augustini et Tabula originalium Gregorii’ (fol. 1v, s. xiv in.) Now
                        partly illegible; supplied by Langbaine‘Liber aule Ballioli et est de ultima
                        eleccione M. J. . .’ (fol. 228)‘ex dono Magistri N. Saxton quondam socii
                        hujus Coll:’ (Langbaine)Notes of pledging (fol. 1): (a) ‘Caucio magistri
                        Willelmi de Eton et Willelmi de Kettylby exposita . . . &lt;die&gt;
                        commemoracionis animarum . . .’; (b) ‘Caucio magistri Willelmi de Eton et
                        Willelmi de Kettylby exposita in cista de Roubery pro sedecim solidis die
                        commemoracionis animarum a.d. millesimo ccc quadragesimo et habet
                        supplementum videlicet Gaufridum super Decretal’’; (c) ‘Caucio magistre
                        Willelmi de Eton et W’; (d) ‘Supplementum communitatis aule de
                     Balliolo’</p></provenance>
                  <provenance type="MLGB3_laterOwners">Apparently given to the college twice, by
                     William Mundham (s. xiv in.) and Nicholas Saxton (d. c. 1471) (CBMLC 16, 1341
                     and 1358)</provenance>
